    "https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2631/phd-position-in-water-footprint-assessment-and-water-credit-design-in-egypts-horticulture-sector/": {
      "title": "PhD position in “Water Footprint Assessment and Water Credit Design in Egypt’s Horticulture Sector”",
      "description": "PhD position in “Water Footprint Assessment and Water Credit Design in Egypt’s Horticulture Sector” - Looking for a job that matters? Vacancies Academic staff Support staff UT Student Jobs UT as employer UT as employer Employment conditions Career and development Pre and onboarding Tenure Track PhD EngD Working as a UT student Stories from UT employees Job alert About UT Campus Research institutes Strategy and culture Twente and Enschede Nederlands English en Nederlands English Vacancies PhD position in “Water Footprint Assessment and Water Credit Design in Egypt’s Horticulture Sector” To vacancy overview Apply now ET PhD PhD position in “Water Footprint Assessment and Water Credit Design in Egypt’s Horticulture Sector” Would you like to study the water-food nexus and contribute to real impact on the ground? Apply for this PhD position, where you will help shape water-smart horticulture in Egypt through the lens of water footprints. Apply now Hi! Are you my new colleague? Mina Shahi Hi! Are you my new colleague? Christopher Balfe Hi! Are you my new colleague? Mark Vlutters Hi! Are you my new colleague? Suzanne Hulscher Hi! Are you my new colleague? Floriana Anselmucci Hi! Are you my new colleague? Tjerkje Dijkstra Hi! Are you my new colleague? Anouk Bomers Hi! Are you my new colleague? Peter Chemweno Key takeaways Hours 40 hr. Salary indication Salary gross/monthly based on full-time € 3,204 - € 4,051 Deadline 1 Nov 2026 The Challenge Egypt’s horticulture sector operates under growing pressure from limited water availability, salinity, and rising competition over finite water resources. At the same time, the sector is economically important for food security, rural livelihoods, and export earnings, which means that improving water productivity is not only an environmental protection measure but also a strategic development and trade challenge. These pressures call for better evidence on current and future water use, stronger metrics for identifying good performance, and more robust ways to link farm-level improvements to wider policy and investment decisions. They also raise questions about how private-sector actors can support and scale water-smart change, including through credible incentive and financing mechanisms. The position You will join the Water Footprint in Action programme, a multi-partner initiative funded by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs and focused on advancing water-smart agriculture in Egypt’s horticulture sector. The programme brings together three complementary lines of work: building a strong scientific and evidence base, strengthening advisory and knowledge systems, and supporting business innovation and investment in water-smart solutions. Within this wider setting, your PhD work will mainly sit in the research and knowledge component, while also helping connect scientific insights to shared knowledge resources, decision-support tools, stakeholder learning, and new financing approaches. A preliminary research plan looks as follows. First, you will develop and apply quantitative approaches to analyse the present and future water consumption (i.e., the water footprint) of Egypt’s horticulture sector. This includes crop modelling using our in-house ACEA model, designing climate and socio-economic scenarios, and linking analyses across scales to local intervention settings, national policy priorities, and trade dynamics. Next, you will work on water footprint benchmarks and performance indicators. In this part of the PhD, you will compare different ways of defining good performance, for example by looking at producer performance based on Best Available Technology and Best Available Practice, and relate these to broader sustainability and efficiency indicators. A third part of your research will focus on how water savings and other water-smart improvements can be measured in a way that is credible, transparent, and useful in practice. You will help develop a science-based method that can underpin incentive or finance mechanisms for improved water performance, working closely with project partners and engaging with wider debates around environmental credits and integrity. You will be embedded in an international consortium and work closely with partners in the Netherlands and Egypt, including Egyptian water and agricultural research centres. The position includes intensive interaction with stakeholders, frequent visits to project locations and case-study sites in Egypt, and an active role in a broader knowledge exchange programme through joint research, data exchange, publications, and learning activities. Your profile You have a Master’s degree in a relevant field, such as water management, agricultural systems, or environmental science. You have a strong quantitative profile, including experience with data analysis, modelling, programming, or computational research methods. You are conceptually strong and able to translate complex sustainability questions into rigorous research designs, including scenario development and method design. You are interested in water footprint assessment, water-smart agriculture, benchmarking, sustainability metrics, and environmental crediting approaches. You enjoy collaborating with international academic and practice partners and can work effectively in a multi-stakeholder environment. You exhibit high levels of self-motivated and have strong communication skills. You are willing to travel and conduct regular project visits in Egypt in connection with research activities, partner collaboration, and case studies. You are motivated to contribute both to high-quality academic research and to applied impact in an international, policy-relevant project setting. Arabic language skills are a strong asset; being an Arabic speaker and having experience in the Egyptian context is beneficial. You are available to start the position per 1 January 2027. Our offer We offer a full-time 4-year PhD-position, with excellent mentorship and a stimulating research environment. We encourage high responsibility and independence, while collaborating with colleagues, researchers, other university staff and partners. The gross monthly salary will be ranging from € 3.204,- (first year), increasing each year up to € 4.051,- in the fourth year. Salary and associated conditions are in accordance with the collective labour agreement for Dutch universities (CAO-NU). You will have a minimum of 232 leave hours in case of full-time employment based on a formal workweek of 38 hours. A full-time employment in practice means 40 hours a week, therefore resulting in 96 extra leave hours on an annual basis. We offer excellent fringe benefits including a holiday allowance of 8% of the gross annual salary, an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. a solid pension scheme, healthcare benefits, free access to sport facilities and a family-friendly institution that offers parental leave (both paid and unpaid). Information and application For additional information regarding this position, you are welcome to contact dr.ir. Rick Hogeboom, h.j.hogeboom@utwente.nl. Please apply by uploading a motivation letter (1 page) your CV (max 3 pages) a writing sample (max 1 page e.g., an Abstract of a publication or a one page summary of your master thesis) as well as relevant certificates You can apply until 1 November 2026 using the link below. The application must not exceed 5 pages excluding certificates. The first (online) job interview will take place between 9-13 November 2026. Screening is part of the procedure Apply now Share this vacancy About the organisation At the Faculty of Engineering Technology (ET), we work on engineering for impact: developing smart, sustainable, human-centred and technological solutions for societal challenges. We connect fundamental education, research and practice across five core domains: Asset & Maintenance engineering, Intelligent Manufacturing Systems, Personalised Health Technology, Resilience Engineering, and Sustainable Production, Energy and Resources. We work on education and research in mechanical engineering, civil engineering and industrial design engineering. Together, we learn by making, creating, and innovating, addressing challenges in a solution-oriented way. Quality, connection and inclusivity are the foundation of our culture. In our open community, students, researchers and staff collaborate with industrial and societal partners. This enables us to develop insights, applications and solutions that add value to society. Want to know more Hogeboom, H.J. (Rick) Associate Professor Hogeboom, H.J. (Rick) Associate Professor Do you have questions about this vacancy? Then you can contact Rick for all substantive questions about this position and the application procedure. For general questions about working for the UT, please refer to the chatbot. Contact Phone: +31534893911 Email: h.j.hogeboom@utwente.nl How to apply Step 1 Apply. When you see a vacancy that appeals to you, you can apply online. We ask you to upload a CV and motivation letter and/or list of publications. You will receive a confirmation of receipt by e-mail. Apply now Step 2 Selection. The selection committee will review your application and you will receive a response within 2 weeks after the vacancy has been closed. Step 3 1st interview. The 1st (online or in person) meeting serves as an introduction where we introduce ourselves to you and you to us. You may be asked to give a short presentation. This will be further explained in the invitation. Step 4 2nd interview. In the second interview, we will further discuss the job content, your skills and your talents. Step 5 The offer. If the conversations are positive, you will be made a suitable offer. If applicable, we will sign you up for screening. Your Colleagues Hulscher, S.J.M.H. (Suzanne) Personal page Boogaard, A.H. van den (Ton) Personal page Munnink, K.J.H. (Karen) Personal page About The Faculty ET Curious about what the Faculty of Engineering Technology (ET) stands for? Check out the ET website for more information. Go to the ET website A job that matters Create new opportunities for yourself, your colleagues and our society. Scientist or teacher, administrator or facilitator, thinker or doer, energetic leader or silent support – your work at the University of Twente matters. And you too! Stories from UT'ers Our mission Human Touch At the University of Twente, technology is all about people. We call this High Tech, Human Touch. This same belief is reflected in the way the Human Resources department operates. We believe that a strong organization starts with people who are given the space to grow, take initiative, and make a difference. That is why we are building a working environment in which everyone can thrive. Our mission We are a university of technology Our university is a public institution that serves society. We are accountable to society for the ways in which we use our academic freedom. We are responsible for ensuring that the power of science and technology is harnessed to achieve the best possible impact in a changing world. We cherish our rich tradition of combining technical and social sciences in our five profiling themes: Improving healthcare by personalized technologies; Creating intelligent manufacturing systems; Shaping our world with smart materials; Engineering our digital society; and Engineering for a resilient world. Our mission We help to strengthen society We help society meet the challenges of today and tomorrow. But we are also transparent about what science and technology can and cannot do in finding sustainable solutions. And help translate these solutions into everyday life. Our mission We are sustainable We want our communities to flourish and show resilience, so we seize opportunities for innovation. We are knowledgeable and have an eye for what society needs. Our students and staff receive all the guidance they need in their quest for ecological, social and economic sustainability. “The University of Twente is all about people. Our sustainable technologies help to strengthen society.” Browse all jobs University of Twente Drienerlolaan 5 7522NB Enschede +31(0)53 489 9111 info@utwente.nl Route Quicklinks Scientific Staff Support Staff Contact Follow us LinkedIn RSS Cookies & Privacy Stay informed. After registration you will regularly receive our new vacancies. Subscribe as External applicant UT Employee (will receive internal vacancies) Email address Login Occupation Administrative & facility Assistant professor Associate professor Education EngD Finance HRM IT Lecturer Legal staff Management Marketing and communications PhD Policy and staff PostDoc Professor Research, development, innovation Researcher Technical and laboratory You are signed up for the Job alert Previous Next Sign up"
    },
    "https://utwentecareers.nl/en/vacancies/2634/4-year-postdoc-position-3d-printing-of-polymer-foams-for-drones-resin-formulation/": {
      "title": "4-year Postdoc position: 3D-printing of polymer foams for drones (resin formulation)",
      "description": "4-year Postdoc position: 3D-printing of polymer foams for drones (resin formulation) - Looking for a job that matters? Vacancies Academic staff Support staff UT Student Jobs UT as employer UT as employer Employment conditions Career and development Pre and onboarding Tenure Track PhD EngD Working as a UT student Stories from UT employees Job alert About UT Campus Research institutes Strategy and culture Twente and Enschede Nederlands English en Nederlands English Vacancies 4-year Postdoc position: 3D-printing of polymer foams for drones (resin formulation) To vacancy overview Apply now ET PostDoc 4-year Postdoc position: 3D-printing of polymer foams for drones (resin formulation) Are you passionate realizing the next generation of 3D-printed foams and composites? We are looking for three highly motivated candidates who together push the boundaries in additive manufacturing of lightweight materials. Apply now Hi! Are you my new colleague? Mina Shahi Hi! Are you my new colleague? Mark Vlutters Hi! Are you my new colleague? Anouk Bomers Hi! Are you my new colleague? Christopher Balfe Hi! Are you my new colleague? Floriana Anselmucci Hi! Are you my new colleague? Suzanne Hulscher Hi! Are you my new colleague? Peter Chemweno Hi! Are you my new colleague? Tjerkje Dijkstra Key takeaways Hours 40 hr. Salary indication Salary gross/monthly based on full-time € 4,422 - € 5,760 Deadline 31 Oct 2026 Job description In the context of a NWO-KIC grant “Materials for defense”, we will investigate fluidic/chemical routes enabling a new generation of porous, graded, and composite materials. We are assembling a team of excellent and highly motivated scientists, who will together investigate and advance the fluid mechanics, the resin formulation, the mechanical properties, and process integration during Direct Bubble Writing. This novel additive manufacturing process for polymer foams was recently invented and patented by the University of Twente. The team will closely interact with ten project partners, including National Dutch Research Institutes (NLR and MARIN), the Ministry of Defense, and globally leading industry partners specializing in the chemistry, the methods (design, printing, composites), or key applications (sailing/flying drones). In the final stage of the project, the printed materials will be tested in unmanned airborne/seaborne vehicles. We are looking for a chemist/chemical engineer/materials scientist (4-year Post-doc; this vacancy), leading the formulation challenges of the foam printing resins. You will focus on formulating resins (rather than synthesis), enabling e.g. printing of stiff, light, and dampening parts with minimal post-processing. An understanding of photo-curable systems, resin formulation, fluid mechanics, and/or soft matter is beneficial. The position is hosted at the University of Twente, starting 1 Jan 2027 or as soon as possible after that date. You will closely collaborate with two PhD/PD-level team members who will (1) lead the understanding and development of the fluidic print process, and (2) lead the integration of printed foams with composites and subsequent upscaling. Together, you will fundamentally change how foams are made: From uniform blocks to precisely graded materials at cell level. Based on this understanding, the team will systematically develop methods for integration, scaling, and application of advanced foams and composites. Your profile We seek motivated colleagues who are excited about the scientific, engineering, and collaborative aspects of the project. Ideally, your CV reflects excellent scientific results, an interest broader than your PhD program, and the ability to deliver results with a team. Specifically: • You are an enthusiastic and highly motivated researcher; • You have obtained a PhD degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, or materials science. • You have excellent analytical skills and a strong ability for solution-oriented problem solving. • You have strong interests in additive manufacturing, including connecting the fundamental and applied aspects. • You have experience in (micro)materials characterization, chemical characterization, and/or material visualization techniques. Experience in e.g. resin formulation, microfluidics, and advanced optical analysis techniques are considered as a benefit. • You possess excellent communication skills, including scientific writing and presenting to a specialized or general audience. • You enjoy working in a team. • You have a creative and critical attitude, combined with perseverance and being flexible. • You are fluent in English and preferably also in Dutch. Our offer • You will be appointed for a period of maximum 4 years full-time within a stimulating scientific environment. The university offers a dynamic ecosystem with enthusiastic colleagues. • Your salary and associated conditions are in accordance with the collective labour agreement for Dutch universities (CAO-NU); • Gross salary between € 4.422,- (step 4) and € 5.760,- (step 12) per month depending on experience and qualifications; • Excellent benefits including a holiday allowance of 8% of the gross annual salary, a year-end bonus of 8.3% and a solid pension scheme; • The flexibility to work (partially) from home; • Free access to sports facilities on campus • A minimum of 232 leave hours in case of full-time employment based on a formal workweek of 38 hours. A full-time employment in practice means 40 hours a week, therefore resulting in 96 extra leave hours on an annual basis. • Excellent support for research and facilities for professional and personal development. • We encourage a high degree of responsibility and independence, while collaborating with close colleagues, researchers and other university staff. • We are a family-friendly institution that offers parental leave (both paid and unpaid) and career support for partners. Information and application Are you interested in this position? Please send your application via the 'Apply now' button below before November 1, and include: A cover letter (maximum 2 pages A4), emphasizing your specific interest, qualifications, motivations to apply for this position. A Curriculum Vitae, including a list of all courses attended and grades obtained, and, if applicable, a list of publications and references. Proof of English proficiency (IELTS or TOEFL) Contact details of at least two references For more information regarding this position, please contact Prof. dr. ir. Claas Willem Visser, c.visser@utwente.nl . Screening is part of the procedure Apply now Share this vacancy About the organisation At the Faculty of Engineering Technology (ET), we work on engineering for impact: developing smart, sustainable, human-centred and technological solutions for societal challenges. We connect fundamental education, research and practice across five core domains: Asset & Maintenance engineering, Intelligent Manufacturing Systems, Personalised Health Technology, Resilience Engineering, and Sustainable Production, Energy and Resources. We work on education and research in mechanical engineering, civil engineering and industrial design engineering. Together, we learn by making, creating, and innovating, addressing challenges in a solution-oriented way. Quality, connection and inclusivity are the foundation of our culture. In our open community, students, researchers and staff collaborate with industrial and societal partners. This enables us to develop insights, applications and solutions that add value to society. Want to know more Visser, C.W. (Claas Willem) Professor (Adjunct) Visser, C.W. (Claas Willem) Professor (Adjunct) Do you have questions about this vacancy? Then you can contact Claas Willem for all substantive questions about this position and the application procedure. For general questions about working for the UT, please refer to the chatbot. Contact Phone: +31534894728 Email: c.visser@utwente.nl How to apply Step 1 Apply. When you see a vacancy that appeals to you, you can apply online. We ask you to upload a CV and motivation letter and/or list of publications. You will receive a confirmation of receipt by e-mail. Apply now Step 2 Selection. The selection committee will review your application and you will receive a response within 2 weeks after the vacancy has been closed. Step 3 1st interview. The 1st (online or in person) meeting serves as an introduction where we introduce ourselves to you and you to us. You may be asked to give a short presentation. This will be further explained in the invitation. Step 4 2nd interview. In the second interview, we will further discuss the job content, your skills and your talents. Step 5 The offer. If the conversations are positive, you will be made a suitable offer. If applicable, we will sign you up for screening. Your Colleagues Hulscher, S.J.M.H. (Suzanne) Personal page Boogaard, A.H. van den (Ton) Personal page Munnink, K.J.H. (Karen) Personal page About The Faculty ET Curious about what the Faculty of Engineering Technology (ET) stands for? Check out the ET website for more information. Go to the ET website A job that matters Create new opportunities for yourself, your colleagues and our society. Scientist or teacher, administrator or facilitator, thinker or doer, energetic leader or silent support – your work at the University of Twente matters. And you too! Stories from UT'ers Our mission Human Touch At the University of Twente, technology is all about people. We call this High Tech, Human Touch. This same belief is reflected in the way the Human Resources department operates. We believe that a strong organization starts with people who are given the space to grow, take initiative, and make a difference. That is why we are building a working environment in which everyone can thrive. Our mission We are a university of technology Our university is a public institution that serves society. We are accountable to society for the ways in which we use our academic freedom. We are responsible for ensuring that the power of science and technology is harnessed to achieve the best possible impact in a changing world. We cherish our rich tradition of combining technical and social sciences in our five profiling themes: Improving healthcare by personalized technologies; Creating intelligent manufacturing systems; Shaping our world with smart materials; Engineering our digital society; and Engineering for a resilient world. Our mission We help to strengthen society We help society meet the challenges of today and tomorrow. But we are also transparent about what science and technology can and cannot do in finding sustainable solutions. And help translate these solutions into everyday life. Our mission We are sustainable We want our communities to flourish and show resilience, so we seize opportunities for innovation. We are knowledgeable and have an eye for what society needs. Our students and staff receive all the guidance they need in their quest for ecological, social and economic sustainability. “The University of Twente is all about people. Our sustainable technologies help to strengthen society.” Browse all jobs University of Twente Drienerlolaan 5 7522NB Enschede +31(0)53 489 9111 info@utwente.nl Route Quicklinks Scientific Staff Support Staff Contact Follow us LinkedIn RSS Cookies & Privacy Stay informed. After registration you will regularly receive our new vacancies. Subscribe as External applicant UT Employee (will receive internal vacancies) Email address Login Occupation Administrative & facility Assistant professor Associate professor Education EngD Finance HRM IT Lecturer Legal staff Management Marketing and communications PhD Policy and staff PostDoc Professor Research, development, innovation Researcher Technical and laboratory You are signed up for the Job alert Previous Next Sign up"
